[size=140][u]Smart Minelayer[/u][/size]

Adds the [b]Smart Minelayer[/b] order: the ship lays mines or laser towers in a pattern you design on the map, refills and restocks them on its own, and its friend/foe mines keep fighting while you are away.

[size=130][u]Features[/u][/size]
[list]
[*] [b]Patterns[/b]: circle, square, hexagon, sphere, cube or the X4 logo, around a point in space or around a station or gate, with a radius, a density and a plane orientation. Concentric shapes, parallel layers and an offset from the target build larger fields from one pattern.
[*] [b]Up to nine fields per ship[/b]: each field, called a slot, has its own target, sector, pattern and item count (up to 1000 items). Changing one slot leaves the items of the others in place.
[*] [b]Friend/foe mines or laser towers[/b]: any friend/foe mine or laser tower the ship can carry. Package mines that release a whole cluster at once, such as the Cluster Mine, are left out.
[*] [b]Active while you are away[/b]: the mines detonate on enemy ships while you are far from the field, where the game otherwise leaves them inert. A mine reaches as far as its trigger range, a tracking mine as far as it follows a target.
[*] [b]Automatic refill[/b]: when a slot's losses reach its replacement threshold, the ship flies out and lays the missing items again.
[*] [b]Own restock[/b]: when the ship runs out of items, it buys them on its own. It looks for your own supply ships and stations first, free of charge, near its sector before farther away. With [b]Restock at Other Factions' Stations[/b] it may also buy at other factions' stations, at their price and only as many as you can pay for.
[*] [b]Pattern changes[/b]: items on points the changed pattern keeps stay where they are; the ship collects the others and lays them on the new points. Collected items it does not lay again go back to a station that builds them: as materials to your own station, or, with [b]Restock at Other Factions' Stations[/b], for its build price to another faction's station.
[*] [b]Experience for kills[/b]: when the mines or laser towers of the ship or its wingmen destroy an enemy ship, the pilot and service crew of the ship and of every wingman gain experience, as they would from the game's attack order.
[*] [b]Wingmen[/b]: ships assigned to the minelayer with the [b]Assist[/b] order lay, refill, restock and collect the same fields together with it.
[*] [b]Waiting[/b]: between refills the ship docks at the nearest station in the field's sector that lets it, or waits in open space a few kilometres off the field's edge.
[/list]
[size=130][u]Limitations[/u][/size]
[list]
[*] S, M and L ships only: XL ships are not offered the order.
[*] One kind of item per ship: once the order holds a mine or laser tower, the window keeps it. To lay another kind, give the ship a new order.
[*] Only friend/foe mines: any other mine could hit the minelayer itself while it lays the field.
[*] While you are away, a mine hits the first enemy ship whose flight path came within its reach since the last check, also one that only passed by; there is no hit chance.
[*] A restock that fails five times in a row stops the order with a message. A trip cut short by your own edit of the order or by another order does not count.
[*] The extension patches two game AI scripts, [b]order.assist.xml[/b] and [b]interrupt.attacked.xml[/b], and one mission script, [b]notifications.xml[/b]. The patches are small, but another mod that patches or replaces the same scripts can still conflict with it.
[/list]
