[size=130][u]Installation[/u][/size]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3843065392]Smart Minelayer[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2622]Smart Minelayer[/url]

[size=130][u]Save state[/u][/size]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[size=130][u]Usage[/u][/size]

Select a ship that carries mines or laser towers, open its [b]Behaviour[/b] on the map and choose [b]Smart Minelayer[/b]. Set [b]Target Position[/b] to a point in space, or [b]Target Object[/b] to a station or gate, and confirm. The configuration window for the first slot opens on the map.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/behaviour.png[/img][/spoiler]

In the [b]Deployable[/b] section pick the type, [b]Mines[/b] or [b]Laser Towers[/b], and the item.

In [b]Shape[/b], [b]Concentric Shapes[/b], [b]Parallel Layers[/b] and [b]Offset[/b] design the field. The window shows how many items the slot needs.

In [b]Maintenance[/b] set the [b]Replacement Threshold[/b]: the share of a slot's items that must be lost before the ship refills it, 0 for at once. [b]Restock at Other Factions' Stations[/b] lets the ship buy at stations that are not yours; a new order starts with your last choice.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/config_window.png[/img][/spoiler]

Confirm, and the ship flies to the field and lays it.

To change or delete a ship's slots, right-click it with no other object selected and choose [b]Configure Smart Minelayer[/b] under [b]Orders[/b].

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/context_menu.png[/img][/spoiler]

The window has one tab per slot, and the tab you are on can be changed. [b]Confirm[/b] saves that slot, [b]Reset[/b] brings back its saved values, [b]Close[/b] leaves all slots as they are. While a tab has changes, the other tabs stay inactive until you confirm or reset.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/window_configure.png[/img][/spoiler]

For another field, select the ship, right-click a spot in space, a station or a gate and choose [b]Add Minelayer Position[/b]. It is offered while the ship has at least one confirmed slot and fewer than nine; the first slot always comes from the [b]Behaviour[/b] panel.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/context_add_position.png[/img][/spoiler]

The window opens with a new tab beside the saved ones, and the map marks the new field; up to nine slots, one tab each. The saved tabs are read-only here: [b]Configure Smart Minelayer[/b] changes or deletes them. A target that already has a slot gets one more. [b]Cancel[/b], Escape or closing the map drops the new slot again. A new target in its [b]Behaviour[/b] adds no slot.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/window_add_slot.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_add_slot.png[/img][/spoiler]

After [b]Confirm[/b], [b]Configure Smart Minelayer[/b] shows both slots, one tab each.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/window_two_slots.png[/img][/spoiler]

[b]Delete[/b] removes the slot of the tab you are on: tick [b]Unlock Delete[/b] above the buttons first. Then [b]Collect Items[/b] appears beside it: ticked, the ship and its wingmen collect the slot's items, and those they do not lay again go back to a station as after a pattern change; the window no longer shows the slot, but it stays with the ship until its last item is collected. Left unticked, the items stay in space and are no longer replaced.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/window_delete.png[/img][/spoiler]

Deleting the last slot clears the order's target too: the ship and its wingmen collect the items if asked, then the ship stands by. [b]Configure Smart Minelayer[/b] stays inactive; while items are still being collected its tooltip says so. Set a [b]Target Position[/b] or [b]Target Object[/b] in its [b]Behaviour[/b] and confirm, and the window of the first slot opens again.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/context_menu_no_slots.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/behaviour_standby.png[/img][/spoiler]

Cancelling the window of the first slot, with [b]Cancel[/b], Escape or by closing the map, leaves the ship the same way: no slot, no target, standing by.

Two fields on the map, each beside its slot:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_sphere_towers.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_cube_mines.png[/img][/spoiler]

One minelayer with two slots in the same sector, one tab each:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_one_ship_overview.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_one_ship_circles.png[/img][/spoiler]

Parallel layers stack copies of a flat shape:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_gate_layers.png[/img][/spoiler]

[size=130][u]Options[/u][/size]

An options page is available via the [b]Extension Options[/b] menu. [b]Keep Slots of a Destroyed Minelayer[/b] shows how many game hours (1 by default) the slots of a minelayer destroyed without wingmen are kept before they are dropped; its friend/foe mines keep working either way. The slider is inactive in this version. [b]Debug Level[/b] sets the detail of the extension's log.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img][/spoiler]

